    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0582" n="478" xml:id="pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11 Shanghai/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-29T17:00:00-05:00">February 29, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. Your 100, February 23, 3 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Refrain from including the clause until otherwise instructed.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Department desires, however, to impress upon you and through you upon the
                        American nationals concerned the importance of obtaining, while the evidence
                        is fresh, complete and accurate evidence with respect to any damages
                        suffered by American nationals. This information should indicate the nature
                        and extent of the damage and by whom it was caused, care being taken in
                        connection with this latter point to avoid the possibility of any effort on
                        the part of the contending factions to shift responsibility.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
